(function(E){ const x = E["exam-01"] = E["exam-01"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x01-r2"] = {"id":"x01-r2","patterns":["RA-mind","GT2-career","GT2-safety","PARA-research","PARA-rules"],"title":{"en":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","tr":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","fa":"Reading ۲: متن ۲ (Passage 2) / بخش ۲ (Section 2)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section holds a piece of information, complete a summary with words from the text, and match statements to the researchers who made them.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve ifadeleri onları söyleyen araştırmacılarla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی هر نکته در کدام بخش متن آمده، یک خلاصه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و هر جمله را به پژوهشگری که آن را گفته وصل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes and sentences about a job and a workplace course with one word copied from the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir iş ve bir işyeri kursu hakkındaki notları ve cümleleri metinden kopyalanmış tek bir kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌ها و جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی یک شغل و یک دوره‌ی کاری را با یک کلمه که از متن کپی می‌کنی کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 2: a report with researchers","tr":"Reading Passage 2: araştırmacıların yer aldığı bir rapor","fa":"Reading Passage 2: گزارشی با چند پژوهشگر"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section holds a piece of information, complete a summary with words from the text, and match statements to the researchers who made them.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, bir özeti metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve ifadeleri onları söyleyen araştırmacılarla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی هر نکته در کدام بخش متن آمده، یک خلاصه را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و هر جمله را به پژوهشگری که آن را گفته وصل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Researchers","tr":"Araştırmacı","fa":"پژوهشگر"},"value":"4"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: why we need quiet","tr":"Bu sınav: neden sessizliğe ihtiyacımız var","fa":"این آزمون: چرا به سکوت نیاز داریم"},"intro":{"en":"Passage 2 often reports research on everyday life: health, the mind, education or work. Several named experts give findings and views, which is why matching features is so common here.","tr":"Passage 2 çoğu zaman günlük hayatla ilgili araştırmaları aktarır: sağlık, zihin, eğitim ya da iş. Adı verilen birkaç uzman bulgular ve görüşler sunar; bu yüzden burada özellik eşleştirme çok yaygındır.","fa":"Passage 2 اغلب پژوهش‌هایی درباره‌ی زندگی روزمره را گزارش می‌کند: سلامت، ذهن، آموزش یا کار. چند متخصصِ نام‌برده یافته و نظر می‌دهند و برای همین جورکردنِ ویژگی‌ها این‌جا خیلی رایج است."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x01-r2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-mind","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Noise, health and the brain","tr":"Gürültü, sağlık ve beyin","fa":"سروصدا، سلامت و مغز"},"asks":{"en":"An explanation in lettered sections (A-G) that brings in several researchers, each with a finding or a view. Passage 2 often looks like this: a report on a problem, its effects and possible solutions.","tr":"Harfli bölümlerden (A-G) oluşan, her biri bir bulgu ya da görüşe sahip birkaç araştırmacıya yer veren bir açıklama. Passage 2 çoğu zaman böyledir: bir sorun, etkileri ve olası çözümler üzerine bir rapor.","fa":"یک توضیح در بخش‌های حرف‌دار (A تا G) که چند پژوهشگر را می‌آورد، هر کدام با یک یافته یا نظر. Passage 2 اغلب همین شکل است: گزارشی درباره‌ی یک مشکل، اثرهایش و راه‌حل‌های ممکن."},"fields":["Sections A-G","Researchers A-D","Findings","Opinions","Solutions"],"words":[{"a":"cannot remember","b":"have no memory of","tr":"hatırlayamamak","fa":"یادشان نمی‌آید"},{"a":"conversation","b":"speech / language / words","tr":"konuşma","fa":"گفتگو"},{"a":"not expensive","b":"cheap / costs little","tr":"pahalı değil","fa":"گران نیست"},{"a":"evidence is limited","b":"more research is needed / too early to say","tr":"kanıt sınırlı","fa":"شواهد محدود است"},{"a":"suggests","b":"his work indicates / she argues","tr":"ileri sürer","fa":"نشان می‌دهد / مطرح می‌کند"},{"a":"a physical reaction","b":"the body responds","tr":"fiziksel tepki","fa":"واکنش جسمی"},{"a":"pollution","b":"a pollutant / contamination","tr":"kirlilik","fa":"آلودگی"},{"a":"for certain customers","b":"for people with particular needs","tr":"belirli müşteriler için","fa":"برای مشتری‌های خاص"},{"a":"unpleasant","b":"uncomfortable / disturbing","tr":"hoş olmayan","fa":"ناخوشایند"},{"a":"ban","b":"prohibit / stop by law","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوعیت"},{"a":"automatic","b":"without thinking / you cannot help it","tr":"otomatik","fa":"خودکار"},{"a":"slower progress","b":"fall behind","tr":"daha yavaş ilerleme","fa":"پیشرفت کندتر"}],"traps":[{"en":"Matching information: the question describes the content of one sentence (\"a physical reaction during sleep\"), not the main idea of the section.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirme: soru bölümün ana fikrini değil, tek bir cümlenin içeriğini anlatır (\"uykuda fiziksel tepki\").","fa":"جورکردن اطلاعات: سؤال محتوای یک جمله را توصیف می‌کند («واکنش جسمی در خواب»)، نه ایده‌ی اصلی بخش را."},{"en":"A researcher can appear in two different sections. Read every mention of a name before you match.","tr":"Bir araştırmacı iki farklı bölümde geçebilir. Eşleştirmeden önce bir ismin geçtiği her yeri oku.","fa":"یک پژوهشگر ممکن است در دو بخش مختلف بیاید. قبل از جور کردن، همه‌ی جاهایی را که اسمش آمده بخوان."},{"en":"A summary gap may sit next to a word from a different section. Check that the meaning fits, not only the words.","tr":"Bir özet boşluğu başka bir bölümden bir kelimenin yanında olabilir. Yalnızca kelimelerin değil, anlamın da uyduğunu kontrol et.","fa":"جای خالی خلاصه ممکن است کنار کلمه‌ای از بخش دیگری باشد. ببین معنی هم جور است، نه فقط کلمه‌ها."}],"example":{"text":"\"Dr Mendes found that workers in quiet rooms made fewer mistakes. Professor Clarke doubts that the effect lasts more than a few days.\"","item":"Statement: The benefit may only be short-term. Which researcher says this?","answer":"Clarke","why":{"en":"\"Doubts that the effect lasts more than a few days\" = the benefit may only be short-term.","tr":"\"Etkinin birkaç günden fazla sürdüğünden şüphe ediyor\" = fayda kısa süreli olabilir.","fa":"«شک دارد که اثرش بیش از چند روز بماند» یعنی ممکن است فایده کوتاه‌مدت باشد."}}},{"id":"RA-mind-report","ctx":["RA-mind"],"title":{"en":"Reports on learning, the mind and society","tr":"Öğrenme, zihin ve toplum üzerine raporlar","fa":"گزارش درباره‌ی یادگیری، ذهن و جامعه"},"asks":{"en":"A report on how people learn, think or behave: bilingual children, boredom, play, mixed-ability classes, putting things off. Paragraphs describe research, explanations and practical advice.","tr":"İnsanların nasıl öğrendiği, düşündüğü ya da davrandığı üzerine bir rapor: iki dilli çocuklar, can sıkıntısı, oyun, karma düzeyli sınıflar, işleri erteleme. Paragraflar araştırmaları, açıklamaları ve pratik tavsiyeleri anlatır.","fa":"گزارشی درباره‌ی اینکه آدم‌ها چطور یاد می‌گیرند، فکر می‌کنند یا رفتار می‌کنند: بچه‌های دوزبانه، کسالت، بازی، کلاس‌های چندسطحی، عقب انداختن کارها. پاراگراف‌ها پژوهش‌ها، توضیح‌ها و توصیه‌های کاربردی را شرح می‌دهند."},"fields":["A popular belief challenged","The benefits for older learners","A practical suggestion for teachers","How the research was carried out","Which paragraph mentions the age of the participants?"],"words":[{"a":"a common belief","b":"many people assume / it is widely thought","tr":"yaygın bir inanış","fa":"باوری رایج"},{"a":"challenge","b":"question / cast doubt on","tr":"sorgulamak","fa":"زیر سؤال بردن"},{"a":"evidence","b":"studies show / data suggest","tr":"kanıt","fa":"شواهد"},{"a":"advantage","b":"benefit / gain","tr":"avantaj","fa":"مزیت"},{"a":"practical advice","b":"tips / what teachers can do","tr":"pratik tavsiye","fa":"توصیه‌ی کاربردی"},{"a":"lasting effect","b":"years later / long-term","tr":"kalıcı etki","fa":"اثر ماندگار"},{"a":"participants","b":"volunteers / subjects","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"age group","b":"children aged six to nine","tr":"yaş grubu","fa":"گروه سنی"},{"a":"behaviour","b":"what people do / how they act","tr":"davranış","fa":"رفتار"},{"a":"motivation","b":"the reason people try","tr":"motivasyon","fa":"انگیزه"},{"a":"concentration","b":"focus / attention","tr":"dikkat","fa":"تمرکز"},{"a":"the role of","b":"how ... contributes to","tr":"... -in rolü","fa":"نقشِ"}],"traps":[{"en":"A heading that repeats a word from the paragraph is often wrong. Match the idea, not the word.","tr":"Paragraftaki bir kelimeyi tekrarlayan başlık çoğu zaman yanlıştır. Kelimeyi değil, fikri eşleştir.","fa":"عنوانی که یک کلمه‌ی پاراگراف را تکرار می‌کند اغلب غلط است. ایده را جور کن، نه کلمه را."},{"en":"Matching information can use the same letter twice: one paragraph may answer two questions.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirmede aynı harf iki kez kullanılabilir: bir paragraf iki soruyu cevaplayabilir.","fa":"در جورکردن اطلاعات یک حرف ممکن است دو بار بیاید: یک پاراگراف می‌تواند جواب دو سؤال باشد."}],"example":{"text":"B  It is often said that boredom is simply a waste of time. Recent work suggests the opposite: people who did a dull task before a creative one produced more original ideas than those who went straight to the creative task.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph B:  i  A popular view of boredom questioned   ii  Ways to avoid boredom at work   iii  Why creative tasks are dull","answer":"i","why":{"en":"\"It is often said... Recent work suggests the opposite\" = a common belief challenged.","tr":"\"Sık söylenir... Yeni çalışmalar tersini gösteriyor\" = sorgulanan yaygın bir inanış.","fa":"«اغلب گفته می‌شود... پژوهش‌های تازه خلافش را نشان می‌دهند» = باوری رایج که زیر سؤال رفته."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-mind"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three tasks on one report","tr":"Tek rapor üzerinde üç görev","fa":"سه تمرین روی یک گزارش"},"body":{"en":"Questions 14-17: which section, A-G, contains the information? A letter may be used more than once. Questions 18-21: complete the summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Questions 22-26: match each statement to a researcher, A-D.","tr":"Soru 14-17: bilgi hangi bölümde, A-G? Bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 18-21: özeti metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 22-26: her ifadeyi bir araştırmacıyla eşleştir, A-D.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۴ تا ۱۷: اطلاعات در کدام بخش (A تا G) است؟ یک حرف ممکن است بیش از یک بار بیاید. سؤال‌های ۱۸ تا ۲۱: خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۶: هر جمله را با یک پژوهشگر (A تا D) جور کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"One method per task","tr":"Her görev için bir yöntem","fa":"برای هر تمرین یک روش"},"steps":[{"en":"Sections: turn each question into a kind of detail (an example, a comparison, a reason) and look for that detail, not for a topic.","tr":"Bölümler: her soruyu bir ayrıntı türüne çevir (örnek, karşılaştırma, neden) ve konu değil, o ayrıntıyı ara.","fa":"بخش‌ها: هر سؤال را به یک نوع جزئیات تبدیل کن (مثال، مقایسه، دلیل) و دنبال همان جزئیات بگرد، نه یک موضوع."},{"en":"Summary: find where the summary starts in the text, then read on in order.","tr":"Özet: özetin metinde nerede başladığını bul, sonra sırayla devam et.","fa":"خلاصه: پیدا کن خلاصه از کجای متن شروع می‌شود، بعد به ترتیب جلو برو."},{"en":"Researchers: circle every name in the passage first. A name can appear in more than one section.","tr":"Araştırmacılar: önce metindeki bütün isimleri daire içine al. Bir isim birden fazla bölümde geçebilir.","fa":"پژوهشگرها: اول دور همه‌ی اسم‌های متن خط بکش. یک اسم ممکن است در چند بخش بیاید."},{"en":"Match the meaning of the statement with what that person says, not with words that look the same.","tr":"İfadenin anlamını o kişinin söylediğiyle eşleştir, aynı görünen kelimelerle değil.","fa":"معنی جمله را با حرف همان شخص جور کن، نه با کلمه‌هایی که شبیه به نظر می‌رسند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A detail, not the main idea","tr":"Ana fikir değil, bir ayrıntı","fa":"یک جزئیات، نه ایده‌ی اصلی"},"body":{"en":"In \"which section contains\", the answer is often one sentence inside a section about something else. A section about city parks may also mention, in one sentence, what the repairs cost, and that sentence can be the answer.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm içeriyor\" sorusunda cevap çoğu zaman başka bir konudaki bölümün içinde tek bir cümledir. Şehir parkları hakkındaki bir bölüm, tek bir cümlede onarımların maliyetinden de söz edebilir ve cevap o cümle olabilir.","fa":"در «کدام بخش شامل...» جواب اغلب یک جمله است در دل بخشی که موضوعش چیز دیگری است. بخشی درباره‌ی پارک‌های شهری ممکن است در یک جمله به هزینه‌ی تعمیرها هم اشاره کند و جواب همان جمله باشد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One researcher, step by step","tr":"Bir araştırmacı, adım adım","fa":"یک پژوهشگر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match each statement with the correct researcher, A-D.","text":"\"Dr Kim found that the effect disappeared after a week. Professor Diaz, however, believes the effect lasts for years.\"","item":"Statement: The effect is short-lived. A Kim  B Diaz","answer":"A","walk":[{"en":"Circle both names in the text.","tr":"Metindeki iki ismi de daire içine al.","fa":"دور هر دو اسم در متن خط بکش."},{"en":"\"Short-lived\" = disappears quickly.","tr":"\"Short-lived\" = çabuk kaybolur.","fa":"«short-lived» یعنی زود از بین می‌رود."},{"en":"\"Disappeared after a week\" belongs to Kim: A.","tr":"\"Bir hafta sonra kayboldu\" Kim’e ait: A.","fa":"«بعد از یک هفته از بین رفت» مال کیم است: A."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"A question asks which section contains \"a reason why a problem is often ignored\". What should you look for?","options":["a sentence that explains why, such as one with because or perhaps","the section that uses the word \"problem\" most often","the section with the most researchers"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"You are looking for a kind of detail, a reason, not for a repeated word.","tr":"Tekrarlanan bir kelimeyi değil, bir ayrıntı türünü, yani bir nedeni arıyorsun.","fa":"دنبال یک نوع جزئیات هستی، یعنی یک دلیل، نه یک کلمه‌ی تکراری."}},"remember":{"en":"Look for the kind of detail, read every mention of a name, and copy summary words exactly.","tr":"Ayrıntının türünü ara, bir ismin geçtiği her yeri oku ve özet kelimelerini aynen kopyala.","fa":"دنبال نوع جزئیات بگرد، هر جا اسمی آمده بخوان و کلمه‌های خلاصه را دقیقاً کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x01-r2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 2","title":{"en":"The value of quiet","tr":"Sessizliğin değeri","fa":"ارزش سکوت"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-mind"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.","passage":"The value of quiet\n\nA  For most of human history, the loudest sounds people heard were thunder, animals and each other. Complaints about noise are not new: in nineteenth-century London, the mathematician Charles Babbage campaigned for years against street musicians playing outside his house. But the scale has changed. Today, traffic, aircraft, machines and music follow many of us from the moment we wake up. Health authorities in a number of countries now treat noise as a pollutant in the same way as smoke or chemical waste, and they set limits on how much of it people should be exposed to. Yet noise is still often regarded as an annoyance rather than a risk, perhaps because, unlike dirty air, it leaves no visible mark.\n\nB  The body, however, does not ignore it. Sudden or continuous noise triggers the same reaction as other forms of stress: the heart beats faster, blood pressure rises and stress hormones are released. Remarkably, this happens even during sleep. The sleep scientist Dr Ingrid Solberg recorded the sleep of people living beside a busy road and found that many of them woke briefly dozens of times a night as lorries passed. In the morning, almost none of them could recall having woken at all, and most described their sleep as normal. Over months and years, she suggests, such interrupted nights may add to the risk of heart disease.\n\nC  At work, the problem is less about volume than about content. Open-plan offices became popular partly because they are cheaper to run and partly because managers believed that removing walls would make colleagues talk to each other more. Some studies have found the opposite: when walls come down, many employees put on headphones and send messages instead. Professor Marcus Oyelaran, an occupational psychologist, has spent a decade studying open-plan offices. His experiments suggest that the sound most damaging to concentration is not the hum of air conditioning or even loud machinery, but nearby conversation. The reason, he believes, is that the brain cannot stop itself from processing words. 'You can learn to ignore a drill,' he says, 'but you cannot learn to ignore language, because understanding it is automatic.'\n\nD  Children may be even more affected. Studies of schools close to airports have linked aircraft noise with slower progress in reading, and teachers in such schools report losing several minutes of each lesson while planes pass overhead. According to the education researcher Dr Leila Haddad, many head teachers assume that the only answer is expensive building work. In her view, this is a misunderstanding: carpets, curtains and simple sound-absorbing panels on ceilings can reduce echo in a classroom dramatically, often for less than the price of a few computers.\n\nE  If noise harms the brain, can silence help it? The neuroscientist Dr Tomasz Wierzbicki believes it can. When the brain is not responding to outside sounds, he explains, it turns to its own activity, replaying recent experiences in a way that may help to store them as long-term memories. Experiments with animals have produced encouraging results. Wierzbicki is careful, though, to point out that research on humans is still at an early stage, and that it is too soon to recommend periods of silence as a way of improving memory.\n\nF  Meanwhile, the demand for quiet is growing. Libraries that once removed silent reading rooms to make space for computers are bringing them back. Some supermarkets now hold a weekly quiet hour, turning down music and lights for customers who find busy shops overwhelming, including many people with autism. Hospitals, too, are paying attention: alarms and conversations at night are among the most common complaints of patients, and some wards now dim the lights and ask staff to lower their voices after ten o'clock. Several cities have begun to map their quietest parks and squares and to protect them from new roads. Solberg would like governments to go further. A ban on night flights, she argues, would do more for the health of people living near airports than almost any other single measure.\n\nG  None of this means that the goal is complete silence. In rooms designed to absorb every sound, most people become uncomfortable within minutes; some report hearing their own heartbeat or a ringing in their ears. Oyelaran points out that humans evolved in a world full of natural sound, and that the sounds of wind, water and birds are, for most people, relaxing rather than disturbing. The aim, he says, is not to remove sound from our lives, but to give people more control over the sounds they hear.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 14-17. Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"a comparison between noise and other kinds of pollution","correct":0,"evidence":"in the same way as smoke or chemical waste","why":{"en":"A: authorities treat noise \"in the same way as smoke or chemical waste\".","tr":"A: yetkililer gürültüyü \"duman ya da kimyasal atıkla aynı şekilde\" ele alıyor.","fa":"A: مسئولان با سروصدا «همان‌طور رفتار می‌کنند که با دود یا پسماند شیمیایی»."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"a description of a situation in which people find a lack of sound unpleasant","correct":6,"evidence":"most people become uncomfortable within minutes","why":{"en":"G: in rooms that absorb every sound, \"most people become uncomfortable within minutes\".","tr":"G: Her sesi emen odalarda \"çoğu insan birkaç dakikada rahatsız olur\".","fa":"G: در اتاق‌هایی که همه‌ی صداها را جذب می‌کنند «بیشتر آدم‌ها در چند دقیقه معذب می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-detail","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to a physical response that continues while people are asleep","correct":1,"evidence":"this happens even during sleep","why":{"en":"B: the heart beats faster and blood pressure rises, and \"this happens even during sleep\".","tr":"B: kalp hızlanır, tansiyon yükselir ve \"bu uykuda bile olur\".","fa":"B: قلب تندتر می‌زند و فشار خون بالا می‌رود و «این حتی در خواب هم اتفاق می‌افتد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"match","prompt":"an example of businesses changing conditions for a particular group of customers","correct":5,"evidence":"Some supermarkets now hold a weekly quiet hour","why":{"en":"F: supermarkets turn down music and lights \"for customers who find busy shops overwhelming\".","tr":"F: süpermarketler müziği ve ışıkları \"kalabalık mağazaları bunaltıcı bulan müşteriler için\" kısıyor.","fa":"F: سوپرمارکت‌ها موسیقی و نور را «برای مشتری‌هایی که فروشگاه شلوغ برایشان طاقت‌فرساست» کم می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 18-21. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"Noise at work and at school","questions":[{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Noise at work and at school · According to Oyelaran, the most distracting sound in an office is nearby ___,","accept":["conversation"],"limit":1,"evidence":"but nearby conversation","why":{"en":"Not machinery or air conditioning: \"nearby conversation\".","tr":"Makineler ya da klima değil: \"yakındaki konuşma\".","fa":"نه ماشین‌آلات و نه کولر: «گفتگوی نزدیک»."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"because the brain cannot help processing ___.","accept":["words"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the brain cannot stop itself from processing words","why":{"en":"\"The brain cannot stop itself from processing words\": cannot help = cannot stop itself.","tr":"\"Beyin kelimeleri işlemekten kendini alamaz\".","fa":"«مغز نمی‌تواند جلوی پردازش کلمه‌ها را بگیرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-plural"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Children in schools near ___ have been found to make slower progress","accept":["airports"],"limit":1,"evidence":"schools close to airports","why":{"en":"\"Schools close to airports\": near = close to.","tr":"\"Havalimanlarına yakın okullar\".","fa":"«مدرسه‌های نزدیک فرودگاه‌ها»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"in ___.","accept":["reading"],"limit":1,"evidence":"slower progress in reading","why":{"en":"\"Slower progress in reading.\"","tr":"\"Okumada daha yavaş ilerleme.\"","fa":"«پیشرفت کندتر در خواندن»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 22-26. Look at the following statements (Questions 22-26) and the list of researchers below. Match each statement with the correct researcher, A, B, C or D. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Ingrid Solberg","B Marcus Oyelaran","C Leila Haddad","D Tomasz Wierzbicki"],"questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"match","prompt":"People may not be aware that noise has disturbed their sleep.","correct":0,"evidence":"could recall having woken at all","why":{"en":"Solberg: almost none of them \"could recall having woken at all\".","tr":"Solberg: neredeyse hiçbiri \"uyandığını hatırlayamadı\".","fa":"سولبرگ: تقریباً هیچ‌کدام «یادشان نمی‌آمد که اصلاً بیدار شده‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"match","prompt":"Reducing noise in classrooms does not need to be costly.","correct":2,"evidence":"often for less than the price of a few computers","why":{"en":"Haddad: simple panels work \"for less than the price of a few computers\".","tr":"Haddad: basit paneller \"birkaç bilgisayarın fiyatından daha ucuza\" işe yarıyor.","fa":"حداد: پنل‌های ساده «با هزینه‌ای کمتر از قیمت چند کامپیوتر» جواب می‌دهند."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":24,"kind":"match","prompt":"There is not yet enough evidence to recommend silence for improving memory in people.","correct":3,"evidence":"it is too soon to recommend periods of silence","why":{"en":"Wierzbicki: research on humans is at an early stage; \"it is too soon to recommend\".","tr":"Wierzbicki: insanlar üzerindeki araştırma başlangıç aşamasında; \"önermek için çok erken\".","fa":"ویرژبیتسکی: پژوهش روی انسان در مرحله‌ی اول است؛ «برای توصیه کردن خیلی زود است»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-hedge"]},{"n":25,"kind":"match","prompt":"Sounds of nature are usually calming for people.","correct":1,"evidence":"the sounds of wind, water and birds are","why":{"en":"Oyelaran, in G: natural sounds are \"relaxing rather than disturbing\". His name appears in C and G.","tr":"Oyelaran, G’de: doğal sesler \"rahatsız edici değil rahatlatıcı\". Adı C ve G’de geçiyor.","fa":"اویه‌لاران، در G: صداهای طبیعی «آرامش‌بخش‌اند، نه آزاردهنده». اسمش در C و G آمده."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-samewords"]},{"n":26,"kind":"match","prompt":"One change to air travel would greatly benefit people living near airports.","correct":0,"evidence":"A ban on night flights, she argues","why":{"en":"Solberg, in F: a ban on night flights \"would do more for the health of people living near airports\". A is used twice.","tr":"Solberg, F’de: gece uçuşlarının yasaklanması \"havalimanı yakınında yaşayanların sağlığı için\" en etkili adım. A iki kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"سولبرگ، در F: ممنوعیت پروازهای شبانه «برای سلامت ساکنان نزدیک فرودگاه» بیشترین فایده را دارد. A دو بار به کار می‌رود."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]}]}],"id":"c-x01-r2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A statement says \"Research on this is still at an early stage.\" Which question would it answer?","options":["Who says the effect is proven?","Who says the research is expensive?","Who says the evidence is limited?"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"At an early stage\" = there is not much evidence yet.","tr":"\"Başlangıç aşamasında\" = henüz fazla kanıt yok.","fa":"«در مرحله‌ی اول» یعنی هنوز شواهد زیادی نیست."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"He could not recall having woken.\" To recall is to...","options":["report","remember","repeat"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Recall = remember.","tr":"Recall = hatırlamak.","fa":"recall یعنی به یاد آوردن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"In a matching features task, a researcher’s name appears in sections C and G. What do you do?","options":["Read both sections before matching","Use only the first mention","Use only the section with the most detail"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The statement may match what the person says in either place.","tr":"İfade, kişinin iki yerden birinde söylediğiyle eşleşebilir.","fa":"جمله ممکن است با حرف آن شخص در هر کدام از دو جا جور باشد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Question: \"Which section contains an example of a solution that costs little?\" Section D is about children and noise. Can the answer be D?","options":["No, D is about children","No, solutions are only in the last section","Yes, if one sentence in D gives that example"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Matching information looks for a detail. A section about children can contain a cheap solution (panels and curtains).","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirme bir ayrıntı arar. Çocuklarla ilgili bir bölüm ucuz bir çözüm (paneller ve perdeler) içerebilir.","fa":"جورکردن اطلاعات دنبال جزئیات است. بخشی درباره‌ی بچه‌ها می‌تواند یک راه‌حل ارزان (پنل و پرده) هم داشته باشد."}}],"id":"c-x01-r2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 2: work texts","tr":"GT Reading Section 2: iş metinleri","fa":"GT Reading Section 2: متن‌های کاری"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes and sentences about a job and a workplace course with one word copied from the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir iş ve bir işyeri kursu hakkındaki notları ve cümleleri metinden kopyalanmış tek bir kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌ها و جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی یک شغل و یک دوره‌ی کاری را با یک کلمه که از متن کپی می‌کنی کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: night work and first aid","tr":"Bu sınav: gece işi ve ilk yardım","fa":"این آزمون: کار شبانه و کمک‌های اولیه"},"intro":{"en":"Section 2 is always about the workplace: job adverts, career advice, staff rules, training and safety. The tasks are usually notes, sentences, a table or a flow-chart.","tr":"Section 2 her zaman işyeriyle ilgilidir: iş ilanları, kariyer tavsiyeleri, personel kuralları, eğitim ve güvenlik. Görevler genelde notlar, cümleler, bir tablo ya da bir akış şemasıdır.","fa":"Section 2 همیشه درباره‌ی محیط کار است: آگهی شغل، توصیه‌ی شغلی، قوانین کارکنان، آموزش و ایمنی. تمرین‌ها معمولاً یادداشت، جمله، جدول یا فلوچارت‌اند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x01-r2gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT2-career","GT2-safety","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-career","n":18,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A job advert and a first-aid course","tr":"Bir iş ilanı ve bir ilk yardım kursu","fa":"یک آگهی کار و یک دوره‌ی کمک‌های اولیه"},"asks":{"en":"Section 2 is about work: a job advert with duties, pay and training, and a description of a safety course for employees.","tr":"Section 2 iş hayatıyla ilgilidir: görevleri, ücreti ve eğitimi içeren bir iş ilanı ve çalışanlar için bir güvenlik kursunun tanıtımı.","fa":"Section 2 درباره‌ی کار است: یک آگهی کار با وظیفه‌ها، حقوق و آموزش، و توضیح یک دوره‌ی ایمنی برای کارکنان."},"fields":["Duties","Hours","Pay and benefits","Training","Requirements","Assessment","Certificate"],"words":[{"a":"duties","b":"your main duties will include","tr":"görevler","fa":"وظیفه‌ها"},{"a":"a shift","b":"a fixed period of work, such as 10 p.m. to 6 a.m.","tr":"vardiya","fa":"شیفت کاری"},{"a":"staff discount","b":"a lower price for employees","tr":"personel indirimi","fa":"تخفیف کارکنان"},{"a":"out of date","b":"past its date / expired","tr":"tarihi geçmiş","fa":"تاریخ‌گذشته"},{"a":"valid","b":"can still be used / has not expired","tr":"geçerli","fa":"معتبر"},{"a":"certificate","b":"a document that shows you passed","tr":"sertifika","fa":"گواهی‌نامه"},{"a":"required by law","b":"employers must by law","tr":"yasal olarak zorunlu","fa":"طبق قانون الزامی"},{"a":"two weeks","b":"a fortnight","tr":"iki hafta","fa":"دو هفته"},{"a":"provided","b":"is given to you / is supplied","tr":"sağlanır","fa":"داده می‌شود"}],"traps":[{"en":"The notes use a general word; the text uses a specific one. Copy the text’s word (\"allowance\", not \"money\").","tr":"Notlar genel bir kelime kullanır; metin özel bir kelime. Metindekini kopyala (\"money\" değil \"allowance\").","fa":"یادداشت‌ها کلمه‌ی کلی به کار می‌برند و متن کلمه‌ی دقیق. کلمه‌ی متن را کپی کن («allowance»، نه «money»)."},{"en":"Sentence completion must be grammatical: \"the office stays ___ until 8 pm\" needs an adjective, open.","tr":"Cümle tamamlama dilbilgisine uygun olmalı: \"the office stays ___ until 8 pm\" bir sıfat ister: open.","fa":"کامل کردن جمله باید از نظر دستوری درست باشد: «the office stays ___ until 8 pm» یک صفت می‌خواهد: open."}],"example":{"text":"\"All new drivers spend their first month with a mentor, a senior driver who checks their routes.\"","item":"New drivers are supported by an experienced driver called a ___","answer":"mentor","why":{"en":"\"A mentor, a senior driver\": the note gives the meaning, the text gives the word.","tr":"\"Bir mentor, kıdemli bir sürücü\": not anlamı, metin kelimeyi verir.","fa":"«یک mentor، یک راننده‌ی باسابقه»: یادداشت معنی را می‌دهد و متن کلمه را."}}},{"id":"GT2-career","ctx":["GT2-career"],"title":{"en":"Job and career guides","tr":"İş ve kariyer rehberleri","fa":"راهنمای کار و مسیر شغلی"},"asks":{"en":"Guides for job seekers and employees: CVs, interviews, promotion, resigning, freelance work, apprenticeships. Sentence and note completion test the advice.","tr":"İş arayanlar ve çalışanlar için rehberler: özgeçmiş, mülakat, terfi, istifa, serbest çalışma, çıraklık. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri sınar.","fa":"راهنما برای کارجوها و کارمندها: رزومه، مصاحبه، ترفیع، استعفا، کار آزاد، کارآموزی حرفه‌ای. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Keep your CV to ___ pages.","Research the company before the ___.","Give your employer written ___ when you resign.","Freelancers must keep records for ___."],"words":[{"a":"CV","b":"career summary / résumé","tr":"özgeçmiş","fa":"رزومه"},{"a":"applicant","b":"candidate / person applying","tr":"başvuran","fa":"متقاضی"},{"a":"vacancy","b":"an open job","tr":"açık pozisyon","fa":"موقعیت شغلی خالی"},{"a":"interview","b":"meeting with the employer","tr":"mülakat","fa":"مصاحبه"},{"a":"resign","b":"leave your job / hand in your notice","tr":"istifa etmek","fa":"استعفا دادن"},{"a":"notice period","b":"time between resigning and leaving","tr":"ihbar süresi","fa":"مدت اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"promotion","b":"moving up to a higher job","tr":"terfi","fa":"ترفیع"},{"a":"freelance","b":"self-employed / working for yourself","tr":"serbest","fa":"آزادکار"},{"a":"apprenticeship","b":"training while you work","tr":"çıraklık","fa":"کارآموزی حرفه‌ای"},{"a":"references","b":"people who will recommend you","tr":"referanslar","fa":"معرف‌ها"},{"a":"salary","b":"pay / earnings","tr":"maaş","fa":"حقوق"},{"a":"recent","b":"latest / most up to date","tr":"en son","fa":"جدیدترین"}],"traps":[{"en":"Advice for different stages: \"before the interview\" and \"after the interview\" are different paragraphs.","tr":"Farklı aşamalar için tavsiyeler: \"mülakattan önce\" ve \"mülakattan sonra\" farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"توصیه برای مرحله‌های مختلف: «قبل از مصاحبه» و «بعد از مصاحبه» در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."},{"en":"The gap needs a word from the text, even if a synonym feels more natural.","tr":"Boşluk metinden bir kelime ister; eş anlamlısı daha doğal gelse bile.","fa":"جای خالی کلمه‌ای از متن را می‌خواهد، حتی اگر مترادفش طبیعی‌تر به نظر برسد."}],"example":{"text":"Most employers spend less than a minute on each CV, so keep yours to two pages and put your most recent job first.","item":"Sentence: Put your most ___ job first.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"recent","why":{"en":"\"Put your most recent job first.\" Copy recent; do not change it to \"latest\".","tr":"\"En son işini en başa koy.\" recent kelimesini kopyala; \"latest\" diye değiştirme.","fa":"«جدیدترین شغلت را اول بنویس». کلمه‌ی recent را کپی کن؛ به latest تغییرش نده."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-career"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-career","n":18,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two texts, thirteen gaps","tr":"İki metin, on üç boşluk","fa":"دو متن، سیزده جای خالی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 15-20 are notes on the job advert; Questions 21-27 are sentences about the course. Each answer is ONE WORD ONLY from the text, and the questions follow the order of each text.","tr":"Soru 15-20 iş ilanıyla ilgili notlar; Soru 21-27 kursla ilgili cümleler. Her cevap metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİME ve sorular her metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۵ تا ۲۰ یادداشت‌هایی درباره‌ی آگهی کارند؛ سؤال‌های ۲۱ تا ۲۷ جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی دوره. هر جواب فقط یک کلمه از متن است و سؤال‌ها به ترتیب هر متن جلو می‌روند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Match each heading in the notes to a heading in the text: Pay and benefits, Training.","tr":"Notlardaki her başlığı metindeki bir başlıkla eşleştir: Pay and benefits, Training.","fa":"هر عنوان یادداشت را با یک عنوان متن جور کن: Pay and benefits، Training."},{"en":"Decide the word class: after \"a\" you need a noun; after \"remains\" an adjective.","tr":"Kelime türüne karar ver: \"a\"dan sonra isim; \"remains\"ten sonra sıfat gerekir.","fa":"نوع کلمه را مشخص کن: بعد از «a» اسم لازم است؛ بعد از «remains» صفت."},{"en":"Find the paraphrase of the words around the gap.","tr":"Boşluğun etrafındaki kelimelerin eş anlamlısını bul.","fa":"معادلِ کلمه‌های دور جای خالی را پیدا کن."},{"en":"Read your sentence again: it must be correct English.","tr":"Cümleni yeniden oku: doğru bir İngilizce olmalı.","fa":"جمله‌ات را دوباره بخوان: باید انگلیسی درستی باشد."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The right word in the right form","tr":"Doğru biçimde doğru kelime","fa":"کلمه‌ی درست در شکل درست"},"body":{"en":"Do not change the word to make it fit. If the text says \"overalls\", write overalls, not \"an overall\" or \"clothes\".","tr":"Kelimeyi uydurmak için değiştirme. Metin \"overalls\" diyorsa overalls yaz; \"an overall\" ya da \"clothes\" değil.","fa":"کلمه را برای جور شدن عوض نکن. اگر متن می‌گوید «overalls»، همان overalls را بنویس، نه «an overall» یا «clothes»."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One sentence, step by step","tr":"Bir cümle, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","text":"\"Applications must reach us by Friday. Late applications will not be considered.\"","item":"Applications that arrive after Friday are not ___","answer":"considered","walk":[{"en":"After \"are not\" you need a verb form like considered.","tr":"\"are not\"tan sonra considered gibi bir fiil biçimi gerekir.","fa":"بعد از «are not» یک شکل فعلی مثل considered لازم است."},{"en":"\"Arrive after Friday\" = late.","tr":"\"Cumadan sonra gelen\" = geç.","fa":"«بعد از جمعه برسد» یعنی دیر."},{"en":"Copy considered: one word, same form.","tr":"considered kopyala: tek kelime, aynı biçim.","fa":"considered را کپی کن: یک کلمه، همان شکل."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Sentence: \"Every visitor is ___ with a hard hat.\" Text: \"Hard hats are supplied to all visitors at no cost.\" What do you write (ONE WORD ONLY)?","options":["supply","supplied","given"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Copy the word in the form the text uses: supplied. \"given\" means the same, but it is not in the text.","tr":"Kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle kopyala: supplied. \"given\" aynı anlama gelir ama metinde yok.","fa":"کلمه را با همان شکلی که در متن آمده کپی کن: supplied. «given» همان معنی را دارد، اما در متن نیست."}},"remember":{"en":"Heading to heading, word class first, then copy one word exactly.","tr":"Başlıktan başlığa, önce kelime türü, sonra tek bir kelimeyi aynen kopyala.","fa":"از عنوان به عنوان، اول نوع کلمه، بعد یک کلمه را دقیقاً کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x01-r2-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 2","title":{"en":"Night work and first aid","tr":"Gece işi ve ilk yardım","fa":"کار شبانه و کمک‌های اولیه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT2-career","GT2-safety"],"texts":[{"title":"Night Team Members: FreshWay Supermarket, Bridgefield","kind":"job advert","body":"FreshWay is looking for reliable people to join the night team at our Bridgefield store. No previous experience is needed, as full training is given, but applicants must be aged 18 or over.\n\nThe job\nNight team members work four nights a week, from 10 pm to 6 am. The store closes to the public at midnight, so for the first two hours you may also need to help customers. Your main duties will include:\n• unloading deliveries from the lorries that arrive during the night\n• filling shelves so that the store is ready when it opens at 7 am\n• checking the dates on fresh products and removing anything that is out of date\n• keeping the shop floor and the stockroom clean and tidy\n• reporting any damaged goods to the shift manager\n• using a handheld scanner to record stock levels\n\nYou will need to be fit enough to lift boxes weighing up to 15 kg.\n\nPay and benefits\nThe basic rate is £12.60 an hour. Because the work is at night, all team members also receive a premium of 25% on top of this rate. Other benefits include a 15% staff discount in all FreshWay stores and a free hot meal on every shift. Uniforms and safety shoes are provided, and there is free parking for staff behind the store. After six months, team members can also join the company pension scheme.\n\nTraining\nFor your first two weeks, you will work alongside a buddy, an experienced member of the team who will show you how everything is done.\n\nHow to apply\nPlease complete the online form at the FreshWay careers website. Interviews take place at the store on Wednesdays, and successful applicants can usually start within a fortnight."},{"title":"Emergency First Aid at Work: one-day course","kind":"course description","body":"Every workplace should have people who know what to do if a colleague is injured or suddenly becomes ill. In many organisations, employers are required by law to make sure that a trained first-aider is always available. This one-day course gives staff the skills and the confidence to act in an emergency.\n\nWho is the course for?\nThe course is designed for people who have no previous experience of first aid. It is suitable for every type of workplace, from offices and shops to warehouses and building sites.\n\nWhat does the course cover?\nThe most important part of the day is learning what to do when someone has stopped breathing. Participants practise chest compressions on life-size manikins until they can do them correctly, and they learn how to use a defibrillator, the machine now found in many public buildings. The course also covers how to deal with choking, heavy bleeding, burns and broken bones, and how to keep an unconscious person in a safe position until help arrives.\n\nHow are participants assessed?\nThere is no written exam. Instead, the trainer watches each participant carry out a series of practical tasks during the day. Those who complete these tasks successfully receive a certificate, which remains valid for three years. After that, a further course must be taken. Because skills are quickly forgotten, we also recommend a short refresher session every year.\n\nWho runs the course?\nAll our trainers have worked in emergency services, as paramedics, nurses or fire officers. They bring real examples from their own careers, which participants often say makes the day much easier to remember.\n\nPractical information\nGroups have a maximum of twelve participants, so that everyone has enough time to practise. As much of the day is spent kneeling on the floor, participants should wear comfortable clothing. Tea and coffee are provided, but lunch is not. The course starts at 9 am and finishes at 4.30 pm.\n\nCourses can be run at your own workplace for groups of six or more. Please contact the training office for prices. Places on our public courses, held every month at the training centre in Mill Lane, can be booked online."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 15-20. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Night team member at FreshWay","questions":[{"n":15,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Night team member · main duties: unloading ___ from lorries","accept":["deliveries"],"limit":1,"evidence":"unloading deliveries from the lorries","why":{"en":"\"Unloading deliveries from the lorries that arrive during the night.\"","tr":"\"Gece gelen kamyonlardan teslimatları boşaltmak.\"","fa":"«خالی کردن محموله‌ها از کامیون‌هایی که شب می‌رسند»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":16,"kind":"gap","prompt":"checking the ___ on fresh products","accept":["dates"],"limit":1,"evidence":"checking the dates on fresh products","why":{"en":"\"Checking the dates on fresh products.\"","tr":"\"Taze ürünlerin tarihlerini kontrol etmek.\"","fa":"«چک کردن تاریخ روی محصولات تازه»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Pay · £12.60 an hour, plus a 25% ___ for night work","accept":["premium"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a premium of 25% on top of this rate","why":{"en":"\"A premium of 25% on top of this rate\": the note says \"plus\", the text says \"on top of\".","tr":"\"Bu ücretin üstüne %25 prim\": not \"plus\", metin \"on top of\" diyor.","fa":"«۲۵ درصد اضافه‌پرداخت روی این نرخ»: یادداشت می‌گوید plus و متن on top of."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Benefits · a free hot ___ on every shift","accept":["meal"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a free hot meal on every shift","why":{"en":"\"A free hot meal on every shift.\"","tr":"\"Her vardiyada ücretsiz sıcak yemek.\"","fa":"«یک وعده غذای گرم رایگان در هر شیفت»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Training · for two weeks, work with a ___","accept":["buddy"],"limit":1,"evidence":"you will work alongside a buddy","why":{"en":"\"Work alongside a buddy, an experienced member of the team.\"","tr":"\"Ekibin deneyimli bir üyesi olan bir buddy ile birlikte çalışırsın.\"","fa":"«کنار یک buddy کار می‌کنی، یکی از اعضای باتجربه‌ی گروه»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Applying · interviews are held on ___","accept":["Wednesdays"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Interviews take place at the store on Wednesdays","why":{"en":"\"Interviews take place at the store on Wednesdays.\" Keep the s.","tr":"\"Mülakatlar çarşamba günleri mağazada yapılır.\" s’yi koru.","fa":"«مصاحبه‌ها چهارشنبه‌ها در فروشگاه برگزار می‌شوند». s را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 21-27. Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"sentence","questions":[{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The course is aimed at people who have no previous ___ of first aid.","accept":["experience"],"limit":1,"evidence":"who have no previous experience of first aid","why":{"en":"\"Designed for people who have no previous experience of first aid.\"","tr":"\"İlk yardım deneyimi olmayan kişiler için tasarlandı.\"","fa":"«برای کسانی طراحی شده که هیچ تجربه‌ی قبلی در کمک‌های اولیه ندارند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Participants practise chest compressions on life-size ___.","accept":["manikins"],"limit":1,"evidence":"chest compressions on life-size manikins","why":{"en":"\"Life-size manikins\": copy the spelling exactly.","tr":"\"Gerçek boyutlu mankenler\": yazımı aynen kopyala.","fa":"«مانکن‌های اندازه‌ی واقعی»: املایش را دقیقاً کپی کن."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"They are shown how to use a ___.","accept":["defibrillator"],"limit":1,"evidence":"how to use a defibrillator","why":{"en":"\"How to use a defibrillator, the machine now found in many public buildings.\"","tr":"\"Artık birçok kamu binasında bulunan bir defibrilatörün nasıl kullanılacağı.\"","fa":"«طرز استفاده از دستگاه شوک قلبی (defibrillator) که حالا در خیلی از ساختمان‌های عمومی هست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Instead of a written exam, the trainer observes participants doing ___ tasks.","accept":["practical"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a series of practical tasks","why":{"en":"\"No written exam. Instead, the trainer watches... a series of practical tasks.\"","tr":"\"Yazılı sınav yok. Bunun yerine eğitmen... bir dizi uygulamalı görevi izler.\"","fa":"«امتحان کتبی نیست. در عوض مربی... یک سری تمرین عملی را تماشا می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The certificate remains ___ for three years.","accept":["valid"],"limit":1,"evidence":"remains valid for three years","why":{"en":"\"A certificate, which remains valid for three years.\"","tr":"\"Üç yıl geçerli kalan bir sertifika.\"","fa":"«گواهی‌ای که سه سال معتبر می‌ماند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"A ___ session is advised every year.","accept":["refresher"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a short refresher session every year","why":{"en":"\"We also recommend a short refresher session every year\": advised = recommended.","tr":"\"Her yıl kısa bir tazeleme dersi öneriyoruz\": advised = recommended.","fa":"«هر سال یک جلسه‌ی کوتاه یادآوری توصیه می‌کنیم»: advised یعنی recommended."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Participants should wear comfortable ___ because they kneel on the floor.","accept":["clothing"],"limit":1,"evidence":"participants should wear comfortable clothing","why":{"en":"\"Participants should wear comfortable clothing.\" \"comfortable\" is printed: write one word.","tr":"\"Katılımcılar rahat kıyafetler giymeli.\" \"comfortable\" yazılı: tek kelime yaz.","fa":"«شرکت‌کننده‌ها باید لباس راحت بپوشند». «comfortable» چاپ شده: یک کلمه بنویس."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x01-r2-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A note says \"extra pay for night work\". Which word in a job advert means this?","options":["premium","discount","pension"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"A premium is an extra amount paid on top of the basic rate.","tr":"Prim, temel ücretin üstüne ödenen ek tutardır.","fa":"premium مبلغی است که روی دستمزد پایه اضافه پرداخت می‌شود."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"An advert says new staff \"can start within a fortnight\". How long is a fortnight?","options":["four weeks","fourteen hours","two weeks"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"A fortnight = two weeks (fourteen nights).","tr":"A fortnight = iki hafta (on dört gece).","fa":"fortnight یعنی دو هفته (چهارده شب)."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Sentence: \"The certificate remains ___ for three years.\" What kind of word do you need?","options":["a noun, like certificate","an adjective, like valid","a verb, like renew"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"After \"remains\", English needs an adjective.","tr":"\"remains\"ten sonra İngilizcede bir sıfat gerekir.","fa":"در انگلیسی بعد از «remains» صفت لازم است."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Uniforms and safety shoes are provided.\" Note: \"Uniform: ___ by the company\" (ONE WORD ONLY). You write...","options":["provided","given","supplied"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Only provided is in the text. Words with the same meaning score nothing.","tr":"Metinde yalnızca provided var. Aynı anlama gelen kelimeler puan almaz.","fa":"فقط provided در متن هست. کلمه‌های هم‌معنی نمره ندارند."}}],"id":"c-x01-r2-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r2"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
